        ]
      },
      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "Así que los dos hermanos salieron a buscarlas, hasta donde las enredaderas cuelgan del cielo.",
          "en": "So the two brothers set out, to the place where the vines hang down from the sky."
        },
        {
          "es": "Allí estaba sentada una anciana ciega, su abuela. Muchos narradores la llaman Matakerepo.",
          "en": "There sat an old blind woman, their grandmother. Many tellers call her Matakerepo."
        },
        {
          "es": "Estaba contando sus diez raíces de taro, una por una.",
          "en": "She was counting her ten taro roots, one by one."
        },
        {
          "es": "En silencio, Tāwhaki le sacó un taro. Ella contó otra vez: solo nueve.",
          "en": "Quietly, Tāwhaki took one taro away. She counted again: only nine."
        },
        {
          "es": "Él sacó más, hasta que ella supo que alguien estaba allí.",
          "en": "He took more, until she knew someone was there."
        },
        {
          "es": "Entonces Tāwhaki le tocó los ojos, y ella volvió a ver. Reconoció a sus nietos, y lloró.",
          "en": "Then Tāwhaki touched her eyes, and she could see again. She knew her grandsons, and she wept."
        }
      ],
